c(1,'prompt','Assume ordinary users, no extended ACLs or overriding privileges, and searchable parent directories. A file is -rw-r-----, owner alice, group finance. Dave is neither owner nor in finance. What access do these mode bits grant Dave?','Stateauthorization scope.',[u])
c(2,'workedExample','DAC lets an owner grant access within other applicable restrictions. MAC imposes policy the ordinary object owner cannot override. Trusted policy administrators may change labels or policy, and malware can still perform actions that the policy allows. MAC is not a blanket promise that malware can never disclose data.','Removeallrootandmalwareabsoluteclaims.',[mi,s])
c(3,'prompt','In the simplified Bell–LaPadula level model, a subject operating at Secret, with no trusted declassification exception, wants to read Top Secret and write to Unclassified. What do the directional rules allow?','Clearancealone notcurrentoperatinglevel.')
