c(5,'text','This portal checks only a coarse customer role and omits the specific invoice ownership constraint','NotintrinsicRBACinexpressibility.',[rb],1)
c(5,'workedExample','The configured role permits invoice reads, but the portal does not check this invoice against this customer. Add an object-level constraint through the application, policy engine or correctly configured database policies. RBAC itself does not prohibit object-specific permissions or additional constraints.','Correctmodelclaim.',[rb])
c(6,'workedExample','ACL-like representations associate an object with allowed principals. Capability-like tokens convey scoped authority to their holder, subject to validation and applicable restrictions. Delegation, expiration and revocation vary: not all capabilities are short-lived, and an S3 presigned URL still depends on its signing credentials and policy.','Avoidautomaticlifetimes/authorityabsolute.',['https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6750.html'])
c(7,'prompt','Assume an authenticated user object has writable name and role attributes, and db.save persists both with no other validation. This illustrative handler receives {"name":"Eve","role":"admin"}. What happens?\n\n```python\n@app.put("/me")\ndef update_me():\n    for k, v in request.json.items():\n        setattr(current_user, k, v)\n    db.save(current_user)\n```','ORMmightreject;stateexampleassumptions.')
c(7,'explanation','Correct under the stated assumptions. Allow only permitted fields and validate values. Changing a login or recovery email may also require reauthentication and address verification.','Emailnot universallysafeeditable.',option=2)
c(8,'prompt','Under a simplified strict Biba policy, a low-integrity process considers the following operations. Which one violates the directional integrity rules? Ignore other access controls.','SeparateabstractBiba fromactualsandbox.',[mi])
c(8,'explanation','Correct. Writing from low to medium is write-up. Windows MIC also commonly blocks write-up, but has its own label policies and is not the full strict Biba model.','MICdistinction.',[mi],0)
c(8,'workedExample','Low-to-medium write violates no-write-up; same-level reads/writes and read-up do not violate these two directional rules. Other permissions can still deny them. These rules alone do not prove that a real renderer cannot persist or escape; that requires its complete sandbox and broker policy.','Removeblanketpersistenceguarantee.',[mi])
c(9,'workedExample','For this supplied graph: Alice is editor of F, D inherits F editors, and editors can view; she can edit/view D. E has Alice only as direct viewer, so she can view E but not edit it. Inheritance in a real product follows its configured rules and exceptions, not a universal rule for everything in every folder.','NoautomaticGoogleDriveuniversal.',[z])
c(10,'prompt','A multi-tenant SaaS leaks data when queries omit a tenant filter. Which approaches can enforce isolation or help catch regressions before release? Select all that apply.','Testsdetectnot structuralfailclosed.')
c(10,'explanation','Correct when configured correctly: enable RLS, use suitable policies and a non-bypass application role, and supply trustworthy tenant context. Superusers/BYPASSRLS bypass RLS; table owners normally do unless FORCE is used. Some operations, including TRUNCATE, are outside row filtering.','RLSnot everyqueryunconditional.',[pg],0)
c(10,'explanation','Correct as an application control plus review tooling, provided all runtime paths use the layer. Code review and lint alone do not make bypass impossible.','Mandatoryclaimnotproven.',option=1)
c(10,'workedExample','Enforced RLS or a consistently used data-access layer can prevent missing application filters from exposing other tenants. RLS needs correct roles, policies and trustworthy tenant context, including connection-pool reset behaviour. Cross-tenant tests can detect regressions but do not themselves enforce isolation. Reminders and UUIDs leave the missing-filter bug intact.','Clearstructuralvsdetectivecontrols.',[pg,o])
c(11,'explanation','403 is a refusal, not a status restricted to unauthenticated users. A 401 specifically requires an authentication challenge.','Correct401403.',[h],1)
c(11,'text','A uniform 404 avoids confirming existence through a 403-versus-404 distinction','Nouniversalnonenumeration.',[h],3)
c(11,'workedExample','Different statuses for existing-but-forbidden and missing IDs can disclose existence. Returning the same 404 removes that particular signal; it does not remove timing, body-size or other endpoint side channels. HTTP permits concealing a forbidden resource with 404.','Removelearnsnothingguarantee.',[h])
